# Normalise line endings so the repo has one answer regardless of who clones it.
#
# eol=lf rather than the default "native" is the deliberate part. The index
# already stores LF for every text file here, but core.autocrlf=true rewrites
# them to CRLF on checkout, so git warns on every add that it is about to
# change bytes it just read. Pinning the working tree to LF removes the
# conversion entirely instead of hiding the warning.
#
# Nothing in this project cares: it is served as static files, and every
# browser, Netlify and the python http.server all read LF fine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never run EOL conversion on these — it corrupts the bytes.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
